 "origin": "library",
 "summary": "A concentrated book of quality businesses, each sorted by a seven-threshold Classification Test into Compounding Machines (10% cap), Transitional holdings (20% cap) or Disruptive Growth (5% cap), with a Probation Hold for a near miss. The test decides the class (C1); its measurement bases (C4 to C8) are written so that anyone reading the same filings reaches the same archetype. Every buy, sale or reclassification is a logged vote, and a sale needs one of four named reasons.",
 "figures": [
  {
   "id": "nav",
   "label": "Net liquidation",
   "about": "Everything in the account at the broker's marks.",
